  "instance_name": "lesbians_have_sex_cat_meme_mapping",
  "label": "Lesbian sexuality mapped onto feline companionship",
  "description": "The text 'this is how lesbians have sex' is mapped onto the visual of two female cats lying side-by-side on a couch. This creates an analogical mapping where the visual material (two cats) is projected as a crude, sexually suggestive metaphor for lesbian sexual activity, reducing it to an animalistic, instinctual behavior. The mapping is explicit through juxtaposition and relies on the stereotype that female cats are 'natural' or 'animalistic' in their behavior, which is then used to demean and mock lesbian sexuality.",
